<body>
<sec sec-type="intro"><title>Introduction</title>
<p>Bleeding after hip surgery is common <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B1">1</xref>, <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B2">2</xref>.</p>
</sec>
<sec sec-type="methods"><title>Methods</title>
<p>We randomized 240 adults aged &#8805;18 y to tranexamic acid or placebo.</p>
<sec><title>Outcomes</title>
<p>The primary outcome was transfusion; secondary outcomes included major bleeding (<italic>P</italic>&#160;&lt;&#160;0.05 for significance).</p>
</sec>
<sec><title>Statistical analysis</title>
<p>Risk ratios were computed as <inline-formula><alternatives><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>R</mml:mi><mml:mi>R</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math><tex-math>RR</tex-math></alternatives></inline-formula> with 95% CI.</p>
<disp-formula id="E1"><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mml:mi>X</mml:mi></mml:math></disp-formula>
</sec>
</sec>
<sec sec-type="results"><title>Results</title>
<sec><title>Primary outcome</title>
<p>Transfusion occurred in 12% of the tranexamic acid group and 31% of the placebo group (RR 0.39, 95% CI 0.24&#8211;0.62).</p>
</sec>
<sec><title>Secondary outcomes</title>
<p>Major bleeding requiring intervention: see <xref ref-type="table" rid="T1">Table 1</xref>.</p>
<list list-type="bullet"><list-item><p>No thromboembolic events in either group.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Length of stay did not differ.</p></list-item></list>
<table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label>
<caption><title>Outcomes by group</title></caption>
<table frame="hsides" rules="groups">
<col width="40%" span="1"/>
